ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: yellow
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [Fixed-seed PRNG producing identical outputs across processes is the textbook, fully-expected behavior of any deterministic RNG seeded with a constant — not an emergent or surprising phenomenon. The "globally-identical secrets" framing dresses up math.rand.New(rand.NewSource(42)) in security-incident language; the mechanism is trivial once the default seed is known. Clock-decoupling "~31x" is similarly the expected behavior of a frozen walltime — no model needed beyond "constant clock returns constant value." The interesting claim is therefore not the mechanism (mundane) but the SYNTHESIS (composition + un-defendability + spec-conformance); evidence should be weighted accordingly.]
CONFOUNDS: [(1) "Cross-LANGUAGE Rust 10/10 identical" demonstrates ABI-boundary location but is a confirmation of determinism, not an independent CSPRNG-demotion mechanism — same seed → same bytes is tautological; it does not add bits beyond L0. (2) "Sole anomaly across 4 runtimes" conflates default-policy choice with spec-conformance; Wasmtime/Wasmer/Node defaulting to OS entropy is a design convention, not proof that wazero's default violates preview1 text (which the packet itself concedes under residual A). (3) The "generator-propagated amplifier" (knqyf263/go-plugin gen/host.go:145) is presented as a blast-radius multiplier but n=1 generator in an n=9 sample — the amplification factor is unquantified (how many downstream artifacts? unknown). (4) "Un-defendable by correct guest" is true for the preview1 ABI surface but a guest CAN defend by mixing host entropy with guest-side state (timestamp, /dev/urandom via WASI fd, application secret) — the claim should be "no in-ABI capability assertion exists" not "no defense possible."]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [(1) That preview1's "high-quality" + blocking-clause unambiguously entails CSPRNG — the packet itself flags this as strong-but-contestable (residual A). The L1 claim "WASI random_get = CSPRNG-contract" for preview1 is asserted but the text-level evidence is interpretive, not literal. (2) That ROS 2's "default transport" actually exposes wazero with the fixed-seed default in a security-sensitive guest path — adoption is cited but the threat-model linkage (does an ROS 2 deployment actually generate keys via this path?) is not demonstrated in the packet. (3) That v1.12.0 being the latest tag implies maintainer awareness/acceptance — could equally be maintainer-unaware; no issue/PR-thread evidence cited on wazero side post-disclosure attempts.]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [(1) n=9 prevalence sample with 2 unmitigated cases yields a point estimate of 22% but no confidence interval; with n=9 the 95% CI on a binomial is roughly 3%-60% — the "real non-zero signal" is real but the population rate is essentially unconstrained. Residual B acknowledges this; the gap is that GREEN-altitude prevalence claims typically require either a population scan or an explicit CI + sampling-frame justification. (2) 30/30 and 10/10 identical-key counts are appropriate for determinism (any non-zero variance would falsify), but no variance was MEASURED for the negative-control runtimes (Wasmtime/Wasmer/Node) at matched n — the asymmetry is fine for the binary determinism claim but should be noted. (3) Generator-amplifier blast-radius is unquantified: dependents-of-knqyf263/go-plugin count not reported, so the "amplifier" claim is directional not magnitudinal.]
RATIONALE: The mechanism itself is mundane (constant-seeded PRNG → constant output, by definition), so the GREEN case rests entirely on the SYNTHESIS — and the synthesis has two acknowledged soft spots that map directly onto theory/modeling concerns: (a) the preview1 spec-violation reading is interpretive (residual A, conceded), and (b) the prevalence claim has an essentially unconstrained CI (residual B, conceded). The L2 guest-defensibility evidence is genuinely strong (no in-ABI entropy-quality query is a clean negative result), and the cross-runtime anomaly across 4 competitors is well-evidenced. But for a theory/modeling skeptic, "synthesis of known-class hazard" + bounded-signal prevalence + contestable preview1 reading is the textbook YELLOW shape: the claim is honest, the residuals are surfaced straight, and a YELLOW-converge (e.g., narrow the claim to "successor-spec violation + cross-runtime-anomaly + un-defendable-at-ABI" and drop or qualify the preview1-violation + prevalence-magnitude claims) would be the zero-false-green outcome. GREEN would require either (i) authenticated population scan to constrain prevalence, or (ii) a citable preview1-era interpretation (WASI working group thread, security advisory, or reference-impl maintainer statement) that resolves residual A in the claim's favor. Prompt version v001.
